From ae33b89b005c6c4eb216e2df2313879fe293b043 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:14:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] server: draft for grammar-constrained requests by default
 (--spec-grammar on)

Tool-call and JSON-schema requests now speculate by default, which is what
agent traffic needs (27B Vulkan: 13.6 vs 4.47 tok/s). --no-spec-grammar
(env LLAMA_ARG_SPEC_GRAMMAR=0) restores the 2026-09-15 guard.

Evidence for flipping the default: live Vulkan 27B, 17 requests, 0 tag
corruption, 72% accept; fleet smoke 54 PASS / 0 FAIL; K2 on 3 backends
80% accept with valid tool-call args. The corruption the guard was added
for was the SSM_CONV_SPLIT conv-window bug, fixed in 0359ec5d4.

Under --spec-synth-* (bench only) the guard still applies; since the flag
is now on by default the old warning would fire on every synth run, so it
becomes an info line. The server test now asserts drafting by default and
draft_n == 0 with --no-spec-grammar; the test harness option becomes
spec_grammar=True by default. Adds the flag to the server README table and
records the flip in FLEET.md.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BidfYiPxg2nUvGVowCgTPK
